## Agent handoff

Use these repo-local Mantle skills for project workflow and updater recovery.
Use the installed package version and `node_modules/@aotter/mantle/docs/` for
runtime/API behavior. `.mantle/*` files provide context, not a separate
contract.

- [`.agents/skills/mantle-develop/SKILL.md`](.agents/skills/mantle-develop/SKILL.md)
- [`.agents/skills/mantle-plugin/SKILL.md`](.agents/skills/mantle-plugin/SKILL.md)
- [`.agents/skills/mantle-theme/SKILL.md`](.agents/skills/mantle-theme/SKILL.md)
- [`.agents/skills/mantle-update/SKILL.md`](.agents/skills/mantle-update/SKILL.md)

First task after materialization:

```text
Read .mantle/launch-state.json, .mantle/features.json, and .mantle/handoff.md.
Install the pinned dependencies, run the local preview, open {{SITE_URL}}, and
confirm the Worker boots. Then
inspect the manifest. For a typed launch, also inspect its composed homepage
and seed files before making changes.
```

## Commands

- `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` install the pinned dependencies (nothing is installed yet)
- `pnpm dev` local preview on localhost:8787
- `pnpm validate` manifest validation
- `pnpm generate` regenerate the machine-owned RuntimePlan/types module
- `pnpm typecheck` TypeScript check
- `pnpm check` validate + typecheck
- `pnpm run deploy` deploy Worker after provider setup

For a typed launch before auth, edit its `.mantle/overlays/<type>/seed.json`.
After auth, daily content authoring should use the Staff MCP endpoint at
`<SITE_URL>/mcp/staff`. Do not write directly to D1 or KV.

Media uploads are optional. Configure them only when requested, then read
`node_modules/@aotter/mantle/docs/media-uploads.md`.

## Notes

- This repo starts from the shared blank base; its selected type is already
  composed. Do not copy old full starter directories into it.
- Theme work happens later through `mantle:theme`; there is no launch
  theme picker.
- If `kiwa/manifest.json` exists, treat `kiwa/` as this Starter revision's
  offline UI reference palette, not runtime source or a permanent Mantle
  contract. Follow `mantle:theme` when adopting or replacing it.
